      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217630/assets/386b2307d81c8f0aa895a192ac2734a7b24f122edb26229f3f9c10f0941c96e7.png)\n\nThe average rate of change of the curve shown above, over the interval $[0,4]$, is $\\frac{Δy}{Δx}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "From the graph, we can see that $f(0)=-2$ and $f(4)=1.$\n\nApplying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(0)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
