    "q-21120": {
      "dom_id": "step-q21120",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The height $h(t),$ measured in feet, of a plant after $t$ years is given by the expression $h(t)=3{t}^{3/2}-2t.$ What is the average rate of growth over the first $4$ years?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $h(t)=3{t}^{3/2}-2t,$ the height measured in feet, of a plant after $t$ years. To find the average rate of change of $h(t)$ from $t=0$ to $t=4,$ we use the average rate of change formula on the interval $[0,4]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δh}{Δt} & =\\frac{h(b)-h(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{h(4)-h(0)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3({4}^{3/2})-2(4)]-[3({0}^{3/2})-2(0)]}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-8}{4} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average rate of growth is $4$ feet per year.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
