    "q-69666": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69666",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find the interval where the average rate of change of $f(x)$ equals $0$ given the following table of values of $f(x):$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,-5\\,$ | $\\,7\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,-4\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ if and only if $Δf=0.$ So\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & Δf=0 \\\\  & f(b)-f(a)=0 \\\\  & f(b)=f(a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means we have to find an interval  $[a,b]$ such that $f(a)=f(b).$\n\nSince $f(-1)=f(5)=3,$ we conclude that $\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=0$ on the interval $[-1,5].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-69666-a",
